back here at home metro police arresting  an 18 year old they say is responsible  for two deadly shootings alonzo brown is  charged with those crimes police say  both happened near tropicana and boulder  highway one last week the other in may  as victoria saha reports police believe  there could have been more violence if  he wasn't caught  18 year old alonso brown was a suspect  police were looking for ever since he  shot and killed a man coming out of a  convenience store on june 23 quickly  realizing he was connected to a murder  at a bus stop in the same area on may 4.  the  suspect seemed to stalk the victim  there appeared to be a random  killing there wasn't any apparent motive  from what we could tell witness  description showed brown wearing similar  clothing and surveillance footage from  the may 4th and june 23 murder the  footage was grainy metro police used all  their resources to identify brown our  detectives were canvassing in the area  and they identified a person that  matched the description of alonso police  say brown took off running and police  chased him he was arrested on monday and  there were two guns found on him making  police believe brown could have striked  again there's no such thing as getting  away with murder in las vegas during  thursday's press conference captain  corrin praising his team for their quick  thinking and solving homicides in our  area metro says in 2021 their ability to  solve homicides was 95 percent whereas  the national average was 65 percent we  have the best homicide unit in the  country if not the world victoria saha  live local now
 

